/target
Cargo.lock
# Catalog chunks staged by an ingest. Downloads are deleted after each chunk,
# but a run in flight has files here, and a staged catalog (ls-dr10-photoz) can
# be hundreds of GB. None of it belongs in git.
data/catalogs
data/alerts
data/schema
data/lsst_alerts_backup*
__pycache__
/env
.DS_Store
/experimental
*~
scripts/convert2onnx/env/
scripts/convert2onnx/models_input/
scripts/convert2onnx/models_output/
.env
tests/throughput/config.yaml
tests/throughput/cats150.filter.json
logs
*.jsonl
simbad_cache
config.docker.yaml

# --- Bulk data never belongs in git -----------------------------------------
# Catalog ingests, the boompy downloaders and the offline LS DR10 pipeline all
# write large binaries into the working tree. Ignoring by extension rather than
# by directory on purpose: the download path is configurable, so listing
# directories only protects the ones we thought of. A 42 MB archive was
# committed once because .zip was not on this list.
*.gz
*.parquet
*.zip
*.tar
*.tgz
*.tbl
*.dat
*.csv
*.fits
*.fit
*.fz
*.npy
*.h5
*.hdf5
*.feather
*.arrow
*.duckdb
*.avro
*.db

# ...except the artifacts the repo genuinely tracks, all of them reviewed and
# most of them in LFS. Negations, so adding a new one needs an explicit path
# here rather than a `git add -f` nobody sees in review.
!data/ls_footprint_moc.fits
!data/models/
!data/models/**
!data/filters/
!data/filters/**
!tests/data/
!tests/data/**

# boompy's uv-managed virtualenv and test cache; uv.lock IS committed, so the
# image and a developer's checkout resolve to the same versions.
.venv/
.pytest_cache/
